## Deployment Path to Marketplace

```
Step 1: Local Development
├─ Clone repo
├─ bash scripts/build-binaries.sh
├─ cd vscode-extension && npm install
├─ npm run esbuild-watch
└─ code . && F5 to debug

Step 2: Testing
├─ npm test
├─ Manual E2E testing
└─ Verify all 6 platform binaries work

Step 3: Release
├─ Update version in package.json
├─ git tag v0.1.0
└─ git push origin --tags

Step 4: GitHub Actions (Automated)
├─ Builds all binaries
├─ Packages extension
├─ Creates GitHub Release
└─ Publishes to marketplaces

Step 5: Verification
├─ Check GitHub Release
├─ Wait for marketplace sync
└─ Test install from marketplace
```

---

## Key Metrics

### Code Statistics
- **TypeScript:** ~800 lines (extension code)
- **Go:** ~300 lines (poml cmd/mcp already exists)
- **Bash:** ~30 lines (build script)
- **Configuration:** ~200 lines (JSON/YAML)
- **Tests:** ~200 lines (jest templates)
- **Documentation:** ~3,000 lines (POML + Markdown)

### Binary Statistics
- **Per-platform size:** ~15 MB (stripped)
- **Total bundled:** ~100 MB (6 platforms)
- **Install size:** ~15 MB (one platform, user-facing)
- **Build time:** ~30 seconds (all 6 platforms)

### Performance
- **Extension activation:** &lt;1 second
- **Server startup:** 1–2 seconds
- **First MCP call:** 100–500 ms
- **Memory footprint:** 100–150 MB (extension + binary)

---

## Success Criteria (MVP)

✅ **Functionality**
- Extension auto-activates on startup
- Detects .poml files and starts server
- All 6 MCP tools functional
- Graceful error handling

✅ **Distribution**
- All 6 platform binaries built and tested
- Extension packages successfully
- CI/CD fully automated (tag → publish)
- No manual steps required

✅ **Quality**
- &gt;50% test coverage
- ESLint passes
- TypeScript strict mode
- No runtime errors in debug mode

✅ **Documentation**
- User guide (README.md)
- Developer guide (quickstart)
- Distribution strategy (documented)
- Complete reference (this doc)

